 "summary": "This is new material for HamiltonianFloerOperations H3, which explicitly asks to \"use the actual positive symmetric metric/coercivity\" on tame compact windows rather than treating \u03c9(\u00b7,J\u00b7) as a metric; the PR's uniform coercivity lemma and the energy-to-L\u00b2 bounds of du \u2212 X_K do exactly that, and the lemma is there to supply the constants for the Floer statements, so the PR is one topic. It moves H3 itself forward (energy controls the perturbed derivative on the way to raw compactness) rather than adding loose material around it, and I found no duplicate on main.",
